      { mistake: "Answering “Cuénteme” with “porque me gusta”.", whyItFails: "The interviewer asked for a short narrative, not a slogan. The answer gives no evidence that you understand the cargo or have relevant experience.", sayInstead: "Me interesa porque llevo tres años trabajando en atención al cliente y he manejado casos similares." },
      { mistake: "Treating “con mucho gusto” as too much for an interview.", whyItFails: "In Colombian professional settings the phrase is expected courtesy. Avoiding it can make you sound less collaborative, especially in a service-oriented role.", sayInstead: "Con mucho gusto le amplío. / Claro que sí, le doy un ejemplo." },
      { mistake: "Listing qualities without a concrete example.", whyItFails: "“Soy responsable y trabajo bien bajo presión” may be true, but it is too generic. Interviewers need to hear what happened, what you did and what changed.", sayInstead: "Por ejemplo, un cliente llegó molesto, revisé su caso y propuse una solución el mismo día." }
